#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096382 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/id #uuid "b77c065c-3821-513c-9376-6e7108074616" :question/math-academy-id "e-4701" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1 \\\\ y+z=-2 \\\\ -x+2y+z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1 \\\\ y+z=-2 \\\\ z=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=2$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+(2)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-4$ and $z=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-4)+(2)=1\\,⟹\\,x=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5,$ $y=-4,$ and $z=2.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -5,-4,2 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096383 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/id #uuid "7760b6ce-91fb-5ba6-beb2-c244d6a73d69" :question/math-academy-id "e-4702" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=-2 \\\\  & x+y+2z=-1 \\\\  & x+2y+z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get $a_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=-2 \\\\ y=3 \\\\ z=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z,$ and the second equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting these values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(3)+(1)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-6,$ $y=3,$ and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,3,1 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "237aa6f1-4bcf-54d7-a265-35842fd96b97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-12$, $y=6$, and $z=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306995} {:answer/id #uuid "a9b32cd9-62b8-5cda-8c27-344ecb042797" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306996} {:answer/id #uuid "7a77cf3d-adf9-549d-960c-c60db24c45dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-12$, $y=-10$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306997} {:answer/id #uuid "3f210db8-3b25-5f8e-8b04-4326d3813eaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=28$, $y=-6$, and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306998} {:answer/id #uuid "1b2ad833-e3f0-5fe8-9a5e-bce6a9cadabc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=18$, $y=6$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9b32cd9-62b8-5cda-8c27-344ecb042797" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306996} :answer-field/id #uuid "27ead658-1607-5e21-bef8-9859ed283c4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8eff9d12-5ab8-5d85-973e-0e821294f176" :question/math-academy-id "q-130927" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y-z=4 \\\\  & -3x-6y+4z=-8 \\\\  & 3x+7y-z=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z=4 \\\\ y+2z=-2 \\\\ z=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+2(4)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-10$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2(-10)-(4)=4\\,⟹\\,x=28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097101 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f11164d-8d9f-5765-9a0b-77929bf292df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307001} {:answer/id #uuid "67435312-eb67-5905-aa86-4ed7396f811d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307002} {:answer/id #uuid "4b9e9171-4fe4-5f65-8e31-b351528e57dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307003} {:answer/id #uuid "fb2c7e25-3a87-51b4-a859-ee1b16c549b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307004} {:answer/id #uuid "cace9311-fc3b-579f-9f3c-3451acd3b9cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cace9311-fc3b-579f-9f3c-3451acd3b9cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307005} :answer-field/id #uuid "e04b9ca7-b715-5742-b275-88103b47755f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a19bbe50-faec-58bf-b57a-44ae8f766527" :question/math-academy-id "q-20505" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y+6z=5 \\\\  & y-10z=-11 \\\\  & 4x+8y+13z=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 13 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 13 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{11}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f324857-5627-527f-a666-b47ac7fbadb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307008} {:answer/id #uuid "e718a0ad-267b-524b-96f8-1da5096c206d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307009} {:answer/id #uuid "af11fd63-fb0d-585b-aa7b-8423e1c676b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307010} {:answer/id #uuid "47eee18a-6148-5064-983b-163d0f11a12c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307011} {:answer/id #uuid "86b29af6-6fec-51f1-9b5f-0a9cb4a714b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af11fd63-fb0d-585b-aa7b-8423e1c676b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307010} :answer-field/id #uuid "892b9e91-0ada-580d-9628-fa6872f03a78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a05ecba-dbf9-513d-af2d-03ee8f54c56e" :question/math-academy-id "q-20508" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67156b7a-a78f-53b1-a101-f2287c7a442e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307015} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b46550-522a-528e-91c7-71b123f79d81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307016} {:answer/id #uuid "9489c7df-6e8e-5d3e-9ff2-de5744cf28a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307017} {:answer/id #uuid "1ef3e629-fc44-55e3-992c-f498f578ba99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307018} {:answer/id #uuid "6bf873a6-f0e8-5756-a6f9-86a730d1f3ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9b46550-522a-528e-91c7-71b123f79d81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307016} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9cc96f2-71ab-5883-9973-7d5e80743532" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8557cbac-c9fb-5ae6-8b4f-ab9d7e2cdf03" :question/math-academy-id "q-20515" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y+z=-4 \\\\  & 2x+5y+3z=-10 \\\\  & 3x+6y+4z=-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "833a74c7-6a79-5b27-a262-23c25afa7527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307022} {:answer/id #uuid "b619c9e5-c442-5bc2-8bde-f43426aa74c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307023} {:answer/id #uuid "1fc543af-5aa8-552e-9550-b2e0855a2ada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307024} {:answer/id #uuid "2f93a8f4-ba16-5259-a528-5852d97cbf7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307025} {:answer/id #uuid "4fe989b6-caa2-5cd6-aba3-7fbbcf3a9f7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b619c9e5-c442-5bc2-8bde-f43426aa74c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307023} :answer-field/id #uuid "40bca7a6-a706-5791-91b5-fe08bcd75d2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ebe05898-9b62-5489-8bf9-f004db945a43" :question/math-academy-id "q-20524" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 6 & 21\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 6 & 21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d62a83a2-5949-5c80-b251-d8b57f98e411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-1,y=4$ and $z=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307029} {:answer/id #uuid "27e46dfc-95ae-5910-96da-2cb4e55ebddd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4,y=5$ and $z=-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307030} {:answer/id #uuid "64e2d1b5-6836-5533-bb22-8b5655bae736" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-11,y=4$ and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307031} {:answer/id #uuid "94e9bcbb-a440-5237-9d40-d9b7887bbeda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=13,y=-4$ and $z=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307032} {:answer/id #uuid "e0cfebc0-40c3-5725-b157-1599893c16b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-2,y=4$ and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27e46dfc-95ae-5910-96da-2cb4e55ebddd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4,y=5$ and $z=-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307030} :answer-field/id #uuid "36858ecf-b05d-5ee4-af71-6b15e5748fc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41dc60ae-16df-5d77-80b8-f746d03ba119" :question/math-academy-id "q-20542" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=-3 \\\\  & x+2y+2z=2 \\\\  & 3x+4y+4z=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and hence solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=-3 \\\\  & y=5 \\\\  & z=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. Substituting both $y=5$ and $z=-6$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+5+2(-6)=-3\\,⟹\\,x-7=-3\\,⟹\\,x=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4,$ $y=5,$ and $z=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab1df4f7-b683-58f9-9a53-9ab3b8f3de6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 4$, $y = 5$, and $z = 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095972} {:answer/id #uuid "d48de23d-197f-5638-8f67-022bd20311ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 4$, $y =-5$, and $z = 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095973} {:answer/id #uuid "ef4aec20-6490-5d49-b934-a54e24f45880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 4$, $y = 6$, and $z = 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095974} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b2100b-3e34-5897-a886-74eaa7dc84ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x =-1$, $y = 2$, and $z = 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095975} {:answer/id #uuid "3759267e-7f9c-5109-a8da-b96bba06dc96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 1$, $y =-6$, and $z =-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef4aec20-6490-5d49-b934-a54e24f45880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 4$, $y = 6$, and $z = 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095974} :answer-field/id #uuid "a873c750-ef0d-5d9f-b3a2-06f31ec27870" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cdba1d21-3eaf-575a-9b38-07c8181fcd34" :question/math-academy-id "q-73396" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y+2z=8 \\\\  & -2x+2y-3z=-11 \\\\  & x+z=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z=8 \\\\ y-z=1 \\\\ z=5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=5$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(5)=1\\,⟹\\,y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=6$ and $z=5$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(6)+2(5)=8\\,⟹\\,x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b06bdab-8dde-5ae4-82b6-bdd85432ec26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307036} {:answer/id #uuid "c09a3337-5bdd-5b70-afda-6a915f809f2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=142$, $y=85$, and $z=22$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307037} {:answer/id #uuid "a0fb858d-7410-530c-a535-374f4bf7db06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=9$, $y=9$, and $z=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307038} {:answer/id #uuid "cf67d0ad-a5bc-5246-a10c-473e813e4bb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-33$, $y=-15$, and $z=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307039} {:answer/id #uuid "2d98a077-0d09-5c3c-a4d2-a14130b0985f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-89$, $y=-47$, and $z=-11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b06bdab-8dde-5ae4-82b6-bdd85432ec26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307036} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f992923-2287-5ec0-ad19-e08e3601aa2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "20ff081a-4610-5c30-9be5-fa40ee345274" :question/math-academy-id "q-73579" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & -3x+6y-3z=18 \\\\  & -4x+8y-3z=2 \\\\  & y-4z=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 & -3 & 18 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 & -3 & 18 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z=-6 \\\\ y-4z=-3 \\\\ z=-22,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=-22$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-4(-22)=-3\\,⟹\\,y=-91.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-91$ and $z=-22$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2(-91)+(-22)=-6\\,⟹\\,x=-166.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307041 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24e6fed1-476a-5e48-b079-1921ac3039cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307043} {:answer/id #uuid "8100d4e5-8239-55c1-82b3-13ffcad4aded" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307044} {:answer/id #uuid "4c6e9ba9-4b7d-56e2-a453-f40b03ee0519" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307045} {:answer/id #uuid "70e05e5f-0032-5342-aeb4-8241faa7b956" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307046} {:answer/id #uuid "1309a08f-7d67-5c97-899e-7bf10126abcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70e05e5f-0032-5342-aeb4-8241faa7b956" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307046} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bf4cf26-97d2-516e-84fd-52fee47d4cbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "09ed8746-0452-52a7-a619-929b2d587f13" :question/math-academy-id "q-73580" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 20 & -10 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 20 & -10 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307048 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b44ac0b-f0a6-5169-91fa-ccd943551ea2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-17,12,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307050} {:answer/id #uuid "24bf5c93-01a8-5636-94b1-c4ee5dc208b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨11,-8,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307051} {:answer/id #uuid "fdbf2bac-e66d-5284-aee3-3749274a9cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨39,-28,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307052} {:answer/id #uuid "f9d5d5c5-0faa-553d-8841-fbb325465107" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307053} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ec3980-8f7f-5956-9395-d25572148fdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨25,-18,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdbf2bac-e66d-5284-aee3-3749274a9cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨39,-28,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307052} :answer-field/id #uuid "e845c512-1717-5897-a5f6-26fcd9cc631e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307049}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2165c009-aa54-51cd-9ee0-62e80fd9ad16" :question/math-academy-id "q-73584" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y-2z=3 \\\\ y+5z=-8 \\\\ z=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+5(4)=-8\\,⟹\\,y=-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-28$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(-28)-2(4)=3\\,⟹\\,x=39.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=39$, $y=-28$, and $z=4.$ Or, in vector form $⟨39,-28,4⟩.$"}]}
